preConditionHook:
// The level that was run is the extreme of the lookback bars ending one bar
// before the breaking bar: EL lowest(low, lookback)[2], bars 2..lookback + 1.
// A history reference at a CONSTANT offset, so the built-in stands in the EL
// twin; here it is the Extremes() loop that built-in bottoms out in -- seeded
// at the window's first bar, scanned strictly with the tolerance-carrying
// comparison (see Breakout), so a tie keeps the earliest bar.
//
// Read into locals so exactly one evaluation per bar feeds both conditions.
// The mined candidate wanted a tracked swing-low pivot; a plain window extreme
// replaces it (mechanizability rule) and removes the pivot-confirmation lag.
lvlLow = low[2];
lvlHigh = high[2];
for (int i = 3; i <= (int)lookback + 1; ++i) {
    if (el_lt(low[i], lvlLow)) lvlLow = low[i];
    if (el_gt(high[i], lvlHigh)) lvlHigh = high[i];
}
